# {{name}}

An Axum service built with [Ferrum Alloy](https://github.com/ferrum-edge/ferrum-alloy).
Handlers in `src/lib.rs` are ordinary Axum. Alloy adds configuration, Problem Details errors, health endpoints, limits, graceful shutdown, and request telemetry.

## Run

```bash
cargo run
curl -s localhost:8080/hello
curl -s localhost:8080/readyz
curl -s -X POST localhost:8080/items -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"name":"tea","quantity":2}'
```

Management endpoints (`/livez`, `/readyz`, `/health`, `/metrics`) listen on `127.0.0.1:9090`.

## Test

```bash
cargo test
```

## Check configuration

```bash
ferrum-alloy check --config alloy.toml
```
{{readme_openapi}}
## Generate gateway configuration

```bash
ferrum-alloy edge export --manifest ferrum-service.toml --output edge.yaml
```

The output is reviewable Ferrum Edge file-mode configuration. Nothing is applied to a gateway.
